90:	 *  load so a cold `.envrc` can't outlast a short-timeout command; `0` or
91:	 *  undefined means "no caller clamp" — the load keeps its full `timeoutMs`
92:	 *  budget (a disabled command deadline is NOT a 0 ms load). Centralizing the
93:	 *  clamp here keeps every backend (executeBash, ACP terminal, PTY) on one
94:	 *  contract instead of each re-deriving it. */
95:	callerTimeoutMs?: number;
