104:/**
105: * Load the repo's direnv/devenv env and fold it into a `(command, env)` pair so
106: * every bash backend (one-shot `executeBash`, ACP client terminal, PTY) exposes
107: * the same devenv tools. Encapsulates: load the diff, merge `set` under the
108: * caller's overlay (caller wins), and prepend a regex-gated `unset -v` for
109: * variables the `.envrc` removes (skipping any the caller re-supplied).
110: *
111: * Returns the possibly-prefixed command plus the merged env, or the inputs
112: * unchanged (`env` = `callerEnv`) when direnv is off, absent, or has no `.envrc`.
113: * Pure transform: does NOT layer non-interactive env defaults — that stays the
114: * caller's job (so interactive PTY/ACP paths keep their own env shape).
115: */
